9,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4TJs!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6c6b183e-3747-4740-8b00-ec2e34d95e5c_2070x1221.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4TJs!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6c6b183e-3747-4740-8b00-ec2e34d95e5c_2070x1221.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4TJs!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6c6b183e-3747-4740-8b00-ec2e34d95e5c_2070x1221.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4TJs!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6c6b183e-3747-4740-8b00-ec2e34d95e5c_2070x1221.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg role=\"img\" style=\"height:20px;width:20px\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><title></title><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>我认为对望远镜的认识大概存在三个级别：倍率，口径和精度。下面我对它们一一进行讲解。</p><h3>倍率</h3><p>普通人都以为望远镜的倍率（放大倍数）越大越好，所以他们看那些 8x，10x，12x，32x…… 之类的数字，以为倍率越大越好。</p><p>然而很简单的道理是，倍率只是放大的倍数，而不是清晰度。如果你的图像本来不清晰，放大再多也不能看到更多的细节。这就像手机的“数码变焦”一样，放大只是把照片中间裁剪了一块出来。你会看到大颗粒的像素，却不能看到更多更清晰的细节，反而可能感觉更模糊了。</p><p>所以倍率显然是最初级无知的理解。</p><h3>口径</h3><p>第二个级别的人，可能买过比较好的望远镜，所以他们听说“口径”是比“倍率”重要的参数。很多望远镜选购网站，甚至很多科普网站，都告诉人们望远镜能力的决定因素是口径，而不是倍率。所以很多人以为口径越大的望远镜就越好。</p><p>口径大的…</p>",
  "truncated_body_text": "我认为对望远镜的认识大概存在三个级别：倍率，口径和精度。下面我对它们一一进行讲解。",
